"Apex is the smaller, crescent-shaped northern part of Anesidora, across The Span from F City."
"In Apex the rules on using powers are heavily relaxed, and minor catastrophes are tolerated."
"High-ranking superhumans live, work, learn and experiment in Apex, and superheroes train there."
"Apex holds several universities with hero programs, Celena North among them."
"Each Apex university has affiliated prep high schools."
"Minors and non-Avowed in Apex wear a lanyard badge with an emergency button."
"Avowed carry a version of the Apex badge on their System IDs, so rescuers can prioritize them."
"Big Boom Town is a small Apex neighborhood of high-rank Wrights, full of explosions and robots."
"Car interfaces warn drivers as they near Big Boom Town."
"Hannah Elber's memorial service was held in Apex, at Celena North."
"Apex is sorted by rank more than F City, to keep powerful people from killing fragile ones."
"Crossing halfway over the bridge into Apex puts an Evac Priority card on the interface."
"Apex high schools run the island's hero-prep programs."
"The fanciest gym in Apex, near Celena North, has three buildings, gardens and a vast pool."
"That gym's concrete building warns people off its one-ton kettlebells."
"The gym's medical center gives entrance physicals for Celena North High."
"Li Jean Academy is another Apex school with a hero program."
"A luxury mall in midtown Apex hides a privacy booth styled as a European train suite."
"That booth costs 5,000 Argold or more for six hours, shielded against prying powers."
"Aulia Velra keeps a penthouse in midtown Apex."
"An Apex shopping boulevard in a Chinese-speaking neighborhood narrows into quirky Avowed shops."
"The Informant, Elias, lives in a brick townhouse facing a grassy square in Apex."
"Kitama Tower is a very safe evacuation shelter in Apex."
"Apex evacuation areas include Punta de la Luna, Albatross Cove and Sanjiao Beach."
"The crescent widens around its curve, and downtown Apex lights follow it."
